{"name":"Gold Dust","hex":"#a4803f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gold dust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Gold in the form of very small pieces, or flour gold.","Anything of great value."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold_dust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gold Dust (elephant)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold Dust was a male Asian elephant that resided at the National Zoo in Washington, D.C. from April 30, 1891, until his death. He was indefinitely lent to the National Zoo as a companion for Dunk by the Adam Forepaugh Circus. He is also alleged to have disemboweled a man in Worcester, Massachusetts in 1884."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_Dust_(elephant)","wikidata":"Q5578717"},{"title":"Gold dust day gecko","blocks":[{"text":"The gold dust day gecko is a diurnal species of gecko. It lives in northern Madagascar, the Comoro Islands, and the Mascarene Islands; it has also been introduced to Hawaii and other Pacific islands. It is primarily an arboreal species which can be found in tropical forests and may also associate with human dwellings. The gold dust day gecko feeds on insects and nectar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Gold_dust_day_gecko_%28Phelsuma_laticauda%29_Nosy_Komba.jpg/330px-Gold_dust_day_gecko_%28Phelsuma_laticauda%29_Nosy_Komba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_dust_day_gecko","wikidata":"Q616510"},{"title":"Gold Dust (DJ Fresh song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Gold Dust\" is a song by British-based DJ and record producer DJ Fresh. It is the third single released from his second album Kryptonite."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/25/Freshgolddust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_Dust_(DJ_Fresh_song)","wikidata":"Q2543425"},{"title":"Dust","blocks":[{"text":"Dust is made of fine particles of solid matter. On Earth, it generally consists of particles in the atmosphere that come from various sources such as soil lifted by wind, volcanic eruptions, and pollution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Dust_storm_approaching_Stratford%2C_Texas.jpg/330px-Dust_storm_approaching_Stratford%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dust","wikidata":"Q165632"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Phelsuma_laticauda_distribution.png/500px-Phelsuma_laticauda_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Phelsuma_laticauda_distribution.png/500px-Phelsuma_laticauda_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhelsuma_laticauda_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Gold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg/500px-Gold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Gold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg/1280px-Gold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Gold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg/500px-Gold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Phelsuma laticauda laticauda licking nectar from the 'bird of paradise' flower of Strelitzia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGold_dust_day_gecko_at_flower-edit1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Gold_Dust_Day_Gecko_closeup_hawaii_edit_1.j